  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Water and Energy for Food 2.0</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WE4F 2.0 supports innovative SMEs and start-ups to scale up their innovations in local food value chains. These innovations lead to more efficient water and energy use by companies and farmers active in the food value chain. The activity takes place in nine MENA countries, a region faced with critical challenges related to water scarcity and energy sustainability, exacerbated by the broader impacts of climate change, with disproportionate negative consequences for those at the bottom of the pyramid. Expected outcomes include investment mobilization, job creation and improvements in sustainable water, energy and agricultural management. Furthermore, WE4F 2.0 serves as a stepping-stone for a Sustainable Impact Fund which could scale the impact of this project beyond its duration.</narrative>
  </description>
